{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0048046","isObsolete":false,"name":"apoplast","definition":{"text":"The cell membranes and intracellular regions in a plant are connected through plasmodesmata, and plants may be described as having two major compartments: the living symplast and the non-living apoplast. The apoplast is external to the plasma membrane and includes cell walls, intercellular spaces and the lumen of dead structures such as xylem vessels. Water and solutes pass freely through it."},"history":[{"timestamp":"2026-03-14","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0110165 (cellular anatomical structure)"},{"timestamp":"2026-03-14","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"part of GO:0005576 (extracellular region)"},{"timestamp":"2026-03-14","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0005576 (extracellular region)"},{"timestamp":"2015-12-09","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2010-02-13","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The cell membranes and intracellular regions in a plant are connected through plasmodesmata, and plants may be described as having two major compartments: the living symplast and the non-living apoplast. The apoplast is external to the plasma membrane and includes cell walls, intercellular spaces and the lumen of dead structures such as xylem vessels. Water and solutes pass freely through it."},{"timestamp":"2010-02-13","action":"Deleted","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The protoplasts of cells in a plant are connected through plasmodesmata, and plants may be described as having two major compartments: the living symplast and the non-living apoplast. The apoplast is external to the plasma membrane and includes cell walls, intercellular spaces and the lumen of dead structures such as xylem vessels. Water and solutes pass freely through it."},{"timestamp":"2009-02-25","action":"Added","category":"XREF","text":"Wikipedia:Apoplast"},{"timestamp":"2008-05-13","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The protoplasts of cells in a plant are connected through plasmodesmata, and plants may be described as having two major compartments: the living symplast and the non-living apoplast. The apoplast is external to the plasma membrane and includes cell walls, intercellular spaces and the lumen of dead structures such as xylem vessels. Water and solutes pass freely through it."},{"timestamp":"2008-05-12","action":"Deleted","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The protoplasts of cells in a plant are connected through plasmodesmata, and plants may be described as having two major compartments: the living symplast and the non-living apoplast. The apoplast is external to the plasma membrane and includes cell walls, intercellular spaces and the lumen of dead structures such as xylem vessels. Water and solutes pass freely through it."},{"timestamp":"2008-04-01","action":"Updated","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0005576 (extracellular region)"},{"timestamp":"2003-05-15","action":"Updated","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The protoplasts of cells in a plant are connected through plasmodesmata, and plants may be described as having two major compartments: the living symplast and the non-living apoplast. The apoplast is external to the plasma membrane and includes cell walls, intercellular spaces and the lumen of dead structures such as xylem vessels. Water and solutes pass freely through it."},{"timestamp":"2003-05-14","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"Since the protoplasts of cells in a plant are connected through plasmodesmata, plants may be described as having two major compartments; the living symplast and the non-living apoplast. The apoplast is external to the plasma membrane and includes cell walls, intercellular spaces and the lumen of dead structures such as xylem vessels. Through it water and solutes pass freely."},{"timestamp":"2003-05-14","action":"Added","category":"TERM","text":"apoplast"}],"xRef